From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: do not raise the shell's desktop window when it gets the focus

Purpose: keep XP's taskbar visible when a window closes (the desktop seemed
to close and open again).
Windows behavior: the shell window (SetShellWindow) stays at the bottom of
the z-order; activating it never brings it above other windows.
Wine before: set_input_focus restacks the focused X window Above before
XSetInputFocus. In a virtual desktop every window is an unmanaged child, so
when a folder window closed and Progman got the focus, Progman (as large as
the screen) went above the taskbar in X until something lowered it again.
Change: with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL=1, the shell window gets the focus
without being raised.
Scope: the window GetShellWindow returns, in the external shell mode.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/event.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
index 34cb33e..daa43b3 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -619,9 +619,13 @@ static void set_input_focus( struct x11drv_win_data *data )
     else
         timestamp = CurrentTime;
 
-    /* Set X focus and install colormap */
-    changes.stack_mode = Above;
-    XConfigureWindow( data->display, data->whole_window, CWStackMode, &changes );
+    /* Set X focus and install colormap. The shell's desktop window stays at
+     * the bottom, under the taskbar, as on Windows. */
+    if (!win4wine_external_shell() || data->hwnd != NtUserGetShellWindow())
+    {
+        changes.stack_mode = Above;
+        XConfigureWindow( data->display, data->whole_window, CWStackMode, &changes );
+    }
 
     if (data->embedder)
         xembed_request_focus( data->display, data->embedder, timestamp );
